From 775563b047caba28501e81c25d8273cead624cca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Jezl <john@jezl.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:43:29 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] DIAGNOSTIC (#1284): PD_WITNESS, preempt_disabled[] check
 at schedule()'s resume point

Build option PD_WITNESS, default OFF; off, only empty macros remain and
.text is unchanged. On, schedule() checks, on the path where it switched
and the incoming task resumes after switch_to():

  W1 (resume, before the clear): preempt_disabled[cpu_id()] == 1, read with
     local interrupts masked. The CPU that switched the task in set its
     own flag before its switch window and nothing clears it before the
     task does.
  W2 (exit, after preempt_disabled[now_cpu] = 0): preempt_disabled[cpu_id()]
     == 0, CPU id re-read independently, interrupts masked. The reverted
     #1229 line (clearing the pre-switch CPU's flag) violates this.

Violations are counted per CPU and kind; the first three print the CPU,
the task and both values. The test harness prints the totals after a
run, and after any filtered pass in which the count changed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
